    "notes": "The exact1159x1536LibraryofCongress native TIFF of AbdullahFreres1880–1893albumen print confirms the complete freestanding square tower: broad exposed plinth, paired lower columns, arched entrance, rectangular middle/arched upper openings, deep projecting tier cornices, tapered clock crown with corner ornaments and long narrow flagmast. The printed original caption and matching Commons PD-AbdulHamid/source cph.3b46533record bind photographer, old period, exact subject and catalog/native identity; generic redirected rights page is not used as proof. The existing full restored tower retains this identifying hierarchy across all four current levels. Previously recorded Galataport caretaker factual text independently establishes the exposed lower140cm and two repaired land/sea clocks, not four dials. The historic monochrome original does not establish current paint, exact clock restoration, hidden faces, floral carving, gilt monogram or hour-mark outlines; these remain original bounded medium-fi interpretations, with symmetric unseen walls and approximate dimensions. Full fixed tower/plinth/crown/mast scope retained. Original model, native map, terrain and placement unchanged; mosque, museums, surrounding square, cloth flag and interiors remain outside the original scope. All39current portable/shared/version2context frames inspected; no new geometry or captures claimed."
